<tr class=gbg><td class= msgboard valign=top ><span class=orangetext>RE: Description of this Message Board</span></td><td class= msgboard valign=top>Added password encryption today...may add a date/time stamp too, but haven't decided yet.</td><td align=right class= msgboardgraytext valign=top ><b>shepler</b><br /><font size=-1>06.02.2002<br />14:51</font></td></tr><tr class=ybg><td class= msgboard valign=top ><span class=orangetext>Updated Message board again</span></td><td class= msgboard valign=top>This was only a minor pain, but I added a time and date stamp to the messages in the database. Everything seems to be working without a hich, but I guess I'll see when post this message.</td><td align=right class= msgboardgraytext valign=top ><b>shepler</b><br /><font size=-1>06.02.2002<br />22:04</font></td></tr><tr class=gbg><td class= msgboard valign=top ><span class=orangetext>RE: Description of this Message Board</span></td><td class= msgboard valign=top>This is an OK implementation, but could be a little better, I think...</td><td align=right class= msgboardgraytext valign=top ><b>rasilt</b><br /><font size=-1>06.03.2002<br />00:11</font></td></tr><tr class=ybg><td class= msgboard valign=top ><span class=orangetext>Description of Time/Date stamps</span></td><td class= msgboard valign=top>The time is simply the server time using the date("H:i") function of PHP, and the date is created by the date("m.d.Y"), by using these two functions, the time is 24-Hour clock style, and the date is in the mm.dd.yyyy format.</td><td align=right class= msgboardgraytext valign=top ><b>shepler</b><br /><font size=-1>06.03.2002<br />10:48</font></td></tr></table>
